WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:02.770
Your eyes

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.440
are the same as mine, young man.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.830
<i>I remember...</i>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.830
<i>I remember her.</i>

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.210
Come.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.500
I have been waiting for you.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.990
Episode 5             I Decide Who's Worthy

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.630
What do you mean?

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.990
Who are you?

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.610
Keep calm.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.740
A witch's eyes house magical power.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.990
If thou art not careful, 
thou shalt be bewitched.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.040
You're in the way.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.530
Professor Los!

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.090
Professor Los!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.340
Professor Los!

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.590
A pretender who cannot even use sorcery 
calls herself a witch and stands at your side.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.440
I am exceedingly displeased.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:54.400
Young man, you are exceptional.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.490
Better than the pretender you hold.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:02.340
Better than the insects who 
swarmed to you for your magic.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.240
That's...

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.250
What'd you do to Hort?

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.340
I let my mercenary have her.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.790
In order to recover you from Albus,

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.260
I have gone to great lengths,

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.340
including taking this village, all for you.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.250
Because of me...

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.360
It's my fault...

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.100
<i>I</i> shall love you.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.450
<i>I</i> shall guide you.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.940
If you are with me, no one 
will be able to hurt you.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.910
Young man, come.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.060
I shall take you to a world befitting of you.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.920
How are they not befitting?

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.300
Take Hort.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.680
She was nice to me when there 
was nothing special about me.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.060
She said the thought of me dying scared her.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.600
And Kudo!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.440
He was honest and 
treated everyone the same.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.030
He had the courage not to change 
his blunt disposition for anyone.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.040
Professor Los, too.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:28.700
She cast her treasured staff away for us!

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.870
She gladly taught us 
anything we needed to know.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.500
You were my only memory.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.160
But of all my memories,

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.420
the one I could most do without...

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.570
is you!

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:53.220
You rebuff me? A witch as great as I?

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:57.980
I'll decide who's worthwhile.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.220
And you

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.090
don't qualify!

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:09.760
<i>If I pour all my magic into a spell,</i>

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.450
<i>I might manage to save 
Professor Los at least.</i>

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.420
Bag Do Gla—

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.790
<i>Wh-What?</i>

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.760
I have not felt this in ages.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:57.040
My whole body is surging with magical energy!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.040
Professor... Los...

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.360
Out-of-control casting?

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.300
Self-destructive acts are foolhardy.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.780
I <i>know</i> I have taught thee that.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.800
So you siphoned magical power from him.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.400
Still, long before you complete any sorcery,

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.930
I can cast magic.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.570
So thou thinkest.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.540
Bag Do Glaht!

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.350
Kalpa fire, come forth!

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:24.810
Flare and blaze!

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.150
Professor Los? You can cast magic?

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:31.980
I can cast this level of spell 
by imitating what I saw.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.910
Since I'm a genius.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.480
Chapter of Hunting, final verse!

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.610
Flagis!

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.000
Grant me power!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.750
My name is Loux Krystas!

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.930
Amusing.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.930
I deny your magic.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.150
Grant me power,

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.930
for I am Zero.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.430
Watch your ego, Dawn Witch.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.370
That spell is mine.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.280
It is <i>my</i> magic.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.320
It is <i>my</i> wisdom and <i>my</i> power.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.580
To wield it against me is laughable.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.330
This art you call magic which 
substitutes for sorcery,

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.960
it all began with <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i>.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.520
<i>I</i> am that Zero.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.990
I wrote <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i>.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.530
<i>This is what she meant.</i>

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:37.970
I could let you meet the 
author of the grimoire.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.130
<i>We never stood a chance of winning.</i>

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:48.820
I am she who discerns meaning 
from meaninglessness,

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.870
who creates something from nothing:
 the Mud-Black Witch!

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:09.950
Huh?

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.670
Wh-What <i>is</i> this?

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:13.280
And, starting today,

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:18.930
I am also the witch who will 
supervise you in the field program.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:22.810
By the way, the textbook 
you use at the Academy,

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.650
<i>The Grimoire of Beginning From Zero</i>?
I wrote that as well.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.730
Uh... Um...

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.690
Well done.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:35.700
I welcome you, young mage.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.880
U-Um...

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.320
Didst thou see that, Sayb?

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.220
A real, live magic denial!

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.200
I am so moved!

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.380
My 300 years alive
 have not been for nothing!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.070
Pull it together! Look alive!

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:01.640
'Twas a test, a test!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.560
Thou hast passed!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.360
I... passed?

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.470
Precisely!

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:07.940
Sayb!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.490
Congrats, Sayb!

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:14.980
Hort!

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.560
Hort, you're okay.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.550
If you had agreed to join Zero,

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:28.960
you would've been expelled on the spot.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:29.750
What?

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.380
Everyone in the village was part of it.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.940
They were all testing us.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.010
The father tested me.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.710
He told me to pretend to be on your side

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:42.500
and keep providing information 
to the anti-witch faction.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.360
But the moment I spat in his face,

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.570
he passed me!

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.190
That priest is a pervert for sure.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.400
Who are you calling a pervert?

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:58.650
Allow me to return this.

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:01.410
My dear Ludens!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.260
I missed thee!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:05.410
You figured out that this 
was a test, didn't you?

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:08.580
Of course I did.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.210
The supposed house of a family that 
died wretched deaths two years ago

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:17.840
was clean and had kitchen utensils, 
water, and tea leaves to boot!

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:22.190
And the hanging dolls 
showed not a sign of wear.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.700
It was ridiculous.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.050
Now that you mention it...

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:28.810
I told you the tea leaves were too much.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:34.540
But that was my special blend for relieving 
the exhaustion of a long journey.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.740
Look who else passed.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:41.260
Y-You guys!

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.420
Kudo!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.830
Thank goodness.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.400
You're both all right.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.780
I was tested, too.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:56.050
That guy told me he ate Holt.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.050
Direct your complaints to the priest. 
He wrote the script!

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:07.470
It was necessary to stir up the students' 
rage, fear, and sense of inferiority.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.140
Dawn Witch Loux Krystas,

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.360
though it was part of a test, 
I ask your forgiveness for the insults.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:17.860
Whatever dost thou mean?

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:22.530
As a pretender, I'm afraid 
my memory is lackluster.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.630
Did you just go into labor?

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.540
You weren't hiding a pregnancy 
from me, were you?

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.380
Ow!

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.040
Of course not, third-rate servant!

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:47.060
I just received word from 
Zero via witch's letter.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:52.560
The three remaining students 
I sent to her all passed!

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.270
<i>All</i>?

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.120
But not a single person passed last year.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.440
It's a remarkable feat!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.950
When I heard they were 
attacked by an Arbiter,

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.690
I was uncertain about what I should do.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.950
It seems I was right to believe in them.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:12.460
Well, being in mortal danger together 
probably cultivated some solidarity.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.900
Yeah, you may be onto something there.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.540
It feels odd,

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.100
but if that's the case, I owe 
the Arbiter my gratitude.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.970
Very well. I'll throw him a bone.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.470
<b>Wanted</b>

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.610
And, if we keep him alive, 
we may find a use for him.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:36.980
Dead or Alive

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:36.860
Distribute this to all the mages, the Church 
& Mage Army, and bounty hunters as well.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.980
Wanted Alive

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:37.980
Dead or Alive

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.710
He hurt my students.

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:44.140
I won't let him get off scot-free.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.990
Now, then, raise a glass to the 
first members of the field program!

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.500
{Villagers}Cheers!

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.630
Where'd all these people spring up from?

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.920
To avoid any accidental bean-spilling,

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.100
they were all holed up at home 
until the end of the test.

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.540
The village was littered 
with beans to find, though.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.440
No need to be so harsh, Dawn Witch.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.460
Allow me to congratulate you again.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:18.740
We wholeheartedly sought your expulsion,

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.720
but you prevailed.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.680
Um, question! Question!

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.990
Why did you seek to expel us?

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.240
Because your talent is too great.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:29.490
Huh?

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.970
If an exceptional mage is 
swayed to the path of evil,

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:35.080
it could mean the end of the world.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.630
We opted to test students 
with great potential

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:42.280
to see if they are virtuous,

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.740
and expel them if they fail.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:52.830
The other two students were selected 
to obtain evidence of their treachery.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.430
But you three were different.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:58.140
If any of you sought to destroy the world,

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.190
the devastation might be greater 
than what we've seen in the north.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.690
S-Surely you're exaggerating.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.760
Young antlered woman,

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:11.010
your talent equals that 
of the Mooncaller Witch.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:14.080
In other words,
 the Headmaster of the Academy.

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:20.100
In 10 years' time, you should have the power 
to lay waste to a thousand troops in seconds.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.840
I-I should?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:26.590
Young lizard man, your 
resourcefulness will be fearsome.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:29.440
Your talent for the Chapter of Protection,

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.800
if you continue to develop it,

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.850
will make you a name as the Immortal Mage.

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:36.850
<i>Me</i>?

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.810
And limitless magic...

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:44.060
Not even I can see your pinnacle.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.820
For the next several hundred years,

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.980
you may be the most long-lived mage.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.320
Furthermore, living a long life means

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.740
endless time to sharpen your techniques.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:58.880
Right now, you are this sphere.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.570
However, in time,

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:02.940
your power might pierce anything.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.200
Staggering, isn't it?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.760
I, too, am staggered

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:09.560
by the force of this possibility.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.370
Possibility...

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.310
So then... things won't 
necessarily turn out that way.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.760
Indeed.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.060
If you neglect your training 
and spend your days loafing,

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:25.320
I can't even imagine what 
lackadaisical mages you'll be.

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.630
That is a staggering prospect itself.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.320
Now, then, let's discuss the field program.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:35.660
You will each have a store.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:36.600
A store?

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:37.330
Yes.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:40.990
So that it's easy for the 
villagers to seek your help.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:46.630
By the way, I operate a paltry magic 
shop on the outskirts of town.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.370
I shall give you three days.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:55.890
Use that time to think about what 
kind of store you want to op—

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:56.970
Dig in!

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.980
You'll think better after ya eat!

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:02.740
There!

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:05.730
Don't be shy! I'll keep it comin'.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.360
This isn't... human meat, is it?

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.770
Don't be silly.

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:17.960
Look at the psychological wound you've 
inflicted on these poor kids, killer priest.

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.830
"Killer priest?"

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:24.080
You see, I used to be 
an Arbiter in Dia Ignis.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:28.840
And just so ya know, he can see.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.840
What?!

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:33.160
Then why do you wear that over your eyes?

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.040
For fashion?

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:35.840
Is it fashion?

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:38.620
Light hurts my eyes.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:42.100
I can only remove this at night.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.760
So it's not fashion.

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:48.110
Oh, is the little girl from the church here?

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.020
There was no little girl at the church.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:51.860
But...

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:56.240
If you mean Lilly, she's over 20 years old.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:00.240
No way! But she's smaller than me!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:04.750
She has a timid personality and 
doesn't like large groups of people.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.750
I'll introduce you one of these days.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.730
Um, Professor Zero...

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:16.550
Did <i>you</i> take me to the Academy?

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:19.010
You don't remember?

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.410
It's all right if you don't.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:27.410
If necessary, you'll remember 
when you need to.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:31.330
A store, huh...

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:34.030
Some kind of magic store, too.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.030
Oh, that reminds me. Where's Professor Los?

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:40.780
She said something about visiting 
Professor Zero's store.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:44.340
She wants to read the books 
Professor Zero has written.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:48.500
H-Hey, you two! Look up there!

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:51.990
Is that...?

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:55.820
Kudo.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:11.030
That's...

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:16.880
The Dragon Conqueror King!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:21.910
Saybil, Hort, and Kudo. Are they here?

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:24.160
Yes! Right here!

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.540
The dispatches from the Academy.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.170
Th-Thank you.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:34.050
Dragon Conqueror King, it's been a while.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:37.610
Hey, Heath. You've gotten big.

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:39.800
I've told you not to call 
me "Dragon Conqueror King."

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:44.930
Loosen up. Your name is known worldwide.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:46.650
It's overblown.

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:50.940
In reality, I'm just here 
to handle little errands.

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:53.870
That just shows how 
important the letters are.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.360
"As field program students,

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.740
you are hereby assigned to the witch village.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:08.120
All restrictions on magic are lifted."

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:13.380
Students that haven't even graduated 
are being authorized to use all magic?

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:17.760
That's essentially full authorization 
to engage in battle.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.930
Naturally, the anti-witch faction 
would have things to say.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:22.470
You might call these

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:24.190
top secret dispatches.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.390
Quite befitting of delivery by dragon.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.100
Excuse me!

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:32.900
I, um...

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:37.230
A long time ago, you saved me!

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:40.240
You're the beastfallen who 
was at the freak show.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.660
Y-You remember?

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:47.240
My heart isn't so dead as 
to forget that atrocity.

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.160
I believe you said you wanted 
to join the Church & Mage Army.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:57.170
If I become a mage, 
do you think I could get in?

00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.400
Who knows?

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:04.350
I'm not in charge of recruitment.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:05.690
But...

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.560
You seem like you'd be an asset in my squad.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.360
I have great expectations.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:18.820
Th-Thank you!

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.460
Why?

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:23.660
How come thou didst not call me?

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:27.840
I wanna see a dragon up close!
 I wanna pet it!

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.780
I wanna ride it, if it'd let me!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:34.170
Well, I'm sure there'll be another chance.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:34.170
I wanna ride the dragon! I wanna!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:38.180
But I might not be in the village then!

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:41.790
What is it?

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.510
What's wrong?

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.900
So you're leaving after all.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:50.700
I told you. She was just our escort.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:55.520
Of course, I shall indeed set out 
again in search of entertainment.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.820
'Tis my way of life.

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:05.530
But until I've read all the books here,

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.120
I intend to remain in the village.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.360
In fact...

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:12.750
I'd say it'll take three years.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:15.850
But should I grow bored, I'll leave at once.

00:21:15.850 --> 00:21:16.750
Study!

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.790
I am fond of growth!

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.310
I am fond of change!

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:24.640
As long as you three aim higher, 
I shall lend a hand.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:27.260
For <i>that</i> is my entertainment!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.300
Professor Los...

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:35.520
'Tis too tight!

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:39.900
Enough, you bunch of big babies!

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.150
You're staying, Dawn Witch?

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:51.330
I should not wish to hear that a witch has 
sunk her fangs into my precious ducklings.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:53.310
Fangs?

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:57.910
Thou art suffering magical depletion.

00:21:57.910 --> 00:22:00.420
And a severe case at that.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.920
So you can tell.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:08.680
Sayb would be a godsend to 
a witch in thy condition.

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:11.680
Your suspicions are justified.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:15.680
If you're staying, I should explain.

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:19.140
The young man was born 
with that peculiar trait.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:22.190
Thus, as you fear might happen now,

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:25.820
he was once attacked by 
a witch seeking power.

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:30.240
The young man had his mother 
killed before his eyes,

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:33.280
and the witch who sought power

00:22:33.280 --> 00:22:35.580
perished by magical overload.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:39.830
As a result, he sealed his own memories away.

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:44.530
With no memories, he experienced 
all manner of oppression

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:46.870
as practically a slave.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:51.600
By placing himself in a wretched environment,

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.500
he was punishing himself.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:58.910
The emotional wound he 
suffered is terribly deep.

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:05.360
Thus, I thought it best to give him a new 
lease on life as a student in the Academy

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:07.990
with no memory of what happened.

00:23:09.510 --> 00:23:12.870
But his peculiar trait posed the danger that

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:16.680
his magic would occasionally 
run wildly out of control.

00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:19.580
So thou soughtest his expulsion.

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:23.420
Thou takest, then givest,
 then takest again. How arrogant.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:28.460
Why dost thou seek to 
control his life like this?

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:31.380
He's my nephew.

00:23:31.750 --> 00:23:35.490
Thy nephew?! Then Sayb's father is...

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:38.890
Thirteen.

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:38.890
Thirteen!

00:23:39.760 --> 00:23:43.390
Yes, the one who stole
 <i>The Grimoire of Zero</i> from me

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:46.010
to create a world controlled by witches.

00:23:46.010 --> 00:23:49.900
The one who caused war in the 
Kingdom of Wenias by spreading magic.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:53.070
That extraordinary evil sorcerer.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:09.920
<b>Next Episode
"Knowledge of Ignorance"</b>

00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:58.580
The field program has finally begun.

00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:01.120
The students lament their inexperience,

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.960
and fight to break through the walls they've hit.

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:04.920
Next time:

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.260
"Knowledge of Ignorance."

00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:09.300
The preview's suddenly 
become awfully serious.
